## Why This Is Asked
This probes cross-region real-time reliability, backpressure handling, and semantics trade-offs in a live data plane.

## Key Concepts
- Tail latency monitoring; regional failover
- Backpressure and traffic shaping
- Exactly-once vs at-least-once semantics
- Offset management and idempotent processing
- Chaos testing and post-incident reviews

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo idempotent replay handler
function processEvent(evt){
  const id = evt.id;
  if (processedSet.has(id)) return;
  store.update(evt.payload);
  processedSet.add(id);
  commitOffsets(evt.offset);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate this plan with simulated regional outages?
- What telemetry would you add to quantify readiness and bottlenecks?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesss ability to architect latency-aware, resilient notify pipelines with per-region strategies, idempotence, and controlled degradation.

## Key Concepts
- Per-region traffic shaping, backpressure, local buffering
- Idempotent delivery and deduplication
- Fast-path caching and back-off strategies
- Canary deployments, runbooks, and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple idempotent delivery using Redis
const redis = require('redis');
const client = redis.createClient();

async function deliver(msgId, payload) {
  const key = `notif:${msgId}`;
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    client.setnx(key, 1, (err, res) => {
      if (err) return reject(err);
      if (res === 1) {
        client.expire(key, 3600, () => resolve(smsGateway.send(payload)));
      } else {
        resolve("duplicate");
      }
    });
  });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure and bound tail latency across regions during gateway outages?
- What alerting would you configure to trigger runbooks and rollback?

